  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef ml_kfold_cv(n_samples: int, n_splits: int = 5) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **K-Fold Cross-Validation** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_kfold_cv(n_samples: int, n_splits: int = 5) -> list:\n    folds = np.array_split(np.arange(n_samples), n_splits)\n    return [{'train': np.concatenate([folds[j] for j in range(n_splits) if j != i]).tolist(), 'test': folds[i].tolist()} for i in range(n_splits)]\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
